            "Find a scaled computation you own (projection, interest, resize, unit conversion at two magnitudes). Write relative-band checks at a small and a large scale with the rel justified in comments, plus one exact zero-regime case. Demonstrate that a 5 percent logic error fails the relative band but would pass a naive absolute band.",
